            {
              "message": {
                "text": "evidence:np-podselector"
              },
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "internal/provisioner/templates.go"
                },
                "region": {
                  "endLine": 189,
                  "startLine": 185
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "The provisioned NetworkPolicy's podSelector matches only pods with the label `app: myapp` (config.go:138-140, applied at templates.go:186-188). Per Kubernetes NetworkPolicy semantics, a namespace's default isolation therefore applies only to workloads that opt in by carrying that label; any pod in a freshly created namespace without the label has no ingress or egress restriction at all. The README presents the policy as a blanket default ('Ingress only from the ingress controller; egress only to postgres + DNS'), which overstates its effect. Additionally, the AllowDNS rule (empty namespaceSelector, UDP/53 to all namespaces) gives labeled pods an unrestricted in-cluster DNS channel usable for exfiltration or tunneling through any in-cluster resolver."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:507518fc4b4cde6e0ef2c4d4d189469c00d8addd6eb67e447d185f43195b46f5",
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "c029414dc8074475:1"
          },
          "properties": {
