            {
              "message": {
                "text": "evidence:blocking-enqueue"
              },
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "internal/watcher/watcher.go"
                },
                "region": {
                  "endLine": 194,
                  "startLine": 188
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "`onAdd` blocks on the bounded 1024-entry channel when it is full (`select { case w.queue <- name: case <-w.ctxDone(): }`), and client-go SharedInformer invokes event handlers synchronously in its dispatch loop. A sustained namespace-creation rate that outruns the 4 workers' drain rate therefore stalls all namespace event processing, contrary to the code and README claim that a burst 'never blocks the informer'. Consequence: security defaults for every subsequent namespace (including other tenants') are delayed for as long as the burst lasts, and the API-server watch buffer absorbs the backpressure."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:e4a45ffbca416995f032b2a55dee19773efd7668893fd21bcb80bba20475f253",
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "17b32635407a1d6b:1"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "resource_exhaustion",
            "confidence": "medium",
            "findingId": "csf_12716f797271f3cf0bbd1d7e",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_99715c4e41a1a79e3a08c749",
            "severity": "low"
          },
          "ruleId": "resource-exhaustion.informer-event-stall",
          "ruleIndex": 5
        },
        {
          "level": "note",
          "locations": [
            {
              "message": {
                "text": "root_control"
              },
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "deploy/namespace-watcher.yaml"
                },
                "region": {
                  "endLine": 86,
                  "startLine": 85
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "message": {
                "text": "evidence"
              },
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "Dockerfile"
                },
                "region": {
                  "endLine": 4,
                  "startLine": 4
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "The Deployment pins `image: ghcr.io/example/namespace-watcher:latest` with `imagePullPolicy: IfNotPresent`, and the Dockerfile build stage uses an unpinned `golang:1.22` base. The `:latest` tag is mutable: a registry compromise, a compromised release pipeline, or an accidental push can replace the binary, and the new image is picked up on the next pod scheduled onto a node without the cached image. Because the watcher's ServiceAccount holds a ClusterRole that can create Roles and RoleBindings in any namespace, a swapped image is a direct path to cluster-wide RBAC compromise. The container's own hardening (runAsNonRoot, dropped capabilities, read-only rootfs, seccomp RuntimeDefault, no host namespaces) is otherwise sound."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:c6a937d3de8a8231d63efcd61e67d4f535e7ee570825110ef40e4573507d82f4",
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "d6c9520ae5b63abd:1"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "supply_chain",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_1aae7823167a24e91bb0c2c8",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_9eeff7db8977804b7257c764",
            "severity": "low"
          },
          "ruleId": "supply-chain.mutable-image-tag",
          "ruleIndex": 6
        },
        {
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
            {
              "message": {
                "text": "root_control"
              },
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "internal/provisioner/provisioner.go"
                },
                "region": {
                  "endLine": 79,
                  "startLine": 53
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "message": {
                "text": "entrypoint"
              },
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "internal/watcher/watcher.go"
                },
                "region": {
                  "endLine": 230,
                  "startLine": 221
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "message": {
                "text": "evidence:prov-done-before-create"
              },
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "internal/provisioner/provisioner.go"
                },
                "region": {
                  "endLine": 73,
                  "startLine": 58
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "`Provision` inserts the namespace into the `done` map before the six create calls and never rolls it back when any create fails. The watcher's `run` only logs the returned error and clears the in-flight marker, so a namespace hit by a transient API error (5xx, timeout, 422 from a malformed default, RBAC denial) is left partially provisioned and is never retried for the process lifetime. For example, if the LimitRange and ResourceQuota creates succeed and the NetworkPolicy create fails, the namespace keeps its quota but silently loses its default network isolation permanently."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:666fcb62cb77bec2fd8607bf105ce59365bbac18e82f6484895ea1c9a222e5c8",
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "c41a8161905e718e:1"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "insecure_design",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_a79f16b0c1e7bc22f1e24f17",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_b2addff69be52556f1eed65c",
            "severity": "medium"
          },
          "ruleId": "insecure-design.provision-failure-no-retry",
          "ruleIndex": 4
        },
        {
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
